WEBVTT

00:02:29.288 --> 00:02:31.829
or assigning them to potentially 
dangerous exposures.

00:02:31.871 --> 00:02:35.329
So, why can’t we rely on these studies
to establish causal relationships

00:02:35.371 --> 00:02:37.621
between substances 
and their effects on health?

00:02:37.788 --> 00:02:40.746
The problem is even the best 
conducted epidemiological studies

00:02:40.788 --> 00:02:41.871
have inherent flaws

00:02:41.913 --> 00:02:45.579
precisely because the test subjects
are not randomly assigned to their groups.

00:02:45.621 --> 00:02:47.788
For example, if the cohort
in our herbal study

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:51.579
consisted of people who took
the supplement for health reasons,

00:02:51.621 --> 00:02:54.246
they may have already 
had higher rates of nausea

00:02:54.288 --> 00:02:56.454
than the other people in the sample.

00:02:56.496 --> 00:03:00.413
Or the cohort group could’ve been composed
of people who shop at health food stores